From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: norm_desc: discard error frames without the
 error summary bit

ndesc_get_rx_status() discards CRC, late collision, overflow and
descriptor errors only when RDES0 bit 15 (error summary) is set. The
H616 manual lists bit 15 as reserved. In store-and-forward mode the MAC
drops such frames itself; in threshold mode they reach the ring.

Test the error bits themselves too (no change where the summary bit
works).

Bit 4 is left out, as before. stmmac reads it as the receive watchdog
timeout, which the Synopsys error summary covers. The H616 manual calls
it RX_LENGTH_ERR ("the length of current frame is wrong"), and the
Allwinner BSP driver does not act on it either.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/norm_desc.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/norm_desc.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/norm_desc.c
index 562177f..1dd663f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/norm_desc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/norm_desc.c
@@ -72,7 +72,12 @@ static int ndesc_get_rx_status(struct stmmac_extra_stats *x,
 	if (!(rdes0 & RDES0_LAST_DESCRIPTOR))
 		return rx_not_ls;
 
-	if (unlikely(rdes0 & RDES0_ERROR_SUMMARY)) {
+	/* Do not rely on the error summary alone: the H616 manual lists bit
+	 * 15 as reserved, and in RX threshold mode error frames reach the ring.
+	 */
+	if (unlikely(rdes0 & (RDES0_ERROR_SUMMARY | RDES0_CRC_ERROR |
+			      RDES0_COLLISION | RDES0_OVERFLOW_ERROR |
+			      RDES0_DESCRIPTOR_ERROR))) {
 		if (unlikely(rdes0 & RDES0_DESCRIPTOR_ERROR))
 			x->rx_desc++;
 		if (unlikely(rdes0 & RDES0_SA_FILTER_FAIL))
-- 
